# Line endings for files whose exact bytes matter.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone
# rewrites LF to CRLF in the working copy. For most files that is invisible.
# For these it is not:
#
# SKILL.md files are digest-verified. tools/gen-seo.js computes a sha256 over
# the bytes on disk and publishes it in
# client/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json, and the Agent Skills Discovery
# spec requires clients to REJECT any file whose digest does not match. Render
# builds on Linux and therefore serves LF. Without this rule, a Windows clone
# would generate CRLF digests for bytes that are served as LF, and every skill
# would fail verification — silently, because nothing on our side checks it.
client/skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf

# Generated by tools/gen-seo.js and served verbatim. Pinned to LF so the output
# is identical whoever runs the generator, and so diffs stay reviewable.
client/*.md              text eol=lf
client/builds/*.md       text eol=lf
client/llms.txt          text eol=lf
client/llms-full.txt     text eol=lf
client/robots.txt        text eol=lf
client/sitemap.xml       text eol=lf
client/.well-known/**    text eol=lf
client/api/openapi.json  text eol=lf
